= Psionic Engineering =

{{Plain_Hook
| in_one_sentence    = Psionic Engineering is the discipline of deriving — not inventing — the physical structures, materials, components, and systems that must necessarily exist if the ψ field equation is correct.
| everyday_analogy   = Maxwell wrote four equations. Engineers did not then invent capacitors, antennas, and waveguides by imagination — they derived them as mathematical consequences of those equations. Psionic Engineering does the same thing for the ψ field: it asks what physical objects the equation demands, and then builds them.
