Psionic Engineering is the discipline sitting between [[Psionics]] (field theory) and [[Psi-Tech]] (device catalog). Its role is the engineering science layer: given that the ψ field obeys the equations established in [[Psionics]], what physical structures must necessarily exist? What materials can store, guide, or attenuate ψ? What components are implied by the wave equation's mathematical structure? What tests would falsify the entire framework?

The discipline is modeled explicitly on the historical development of radio-frequency engineering from Maxwell's equations. Maxwell did not design a capacitor. The capacitor is a mathematical consequence of the divergence term in Gauss's law, implemented in hardware. Every mature engineering discipline follows the same progression:

:<math>\text{Field Theory} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Material Science} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Constitutive Relations} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Primitive Components} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Circuits} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Systems} \;\longrightarrow\; \text{Applications}</math>

Psionic Engineering is the formalization of that progression for the ψ field.

