=== The Two-Track Rule ===

Every page in this branch explicitly separates its content into two tracks:

* '''Track A — Established Physics:''' Content that is buildable and testable with existing technology, regardless of whether ψ is real. This includes metamaterial fabrication, TPMS lattice design, bifilar coil engineering, BST composite chemistry, FPGA control loops, and HRV biofeedback. Track A content is marked with no special label — it is standard engineering.

* '''Track B — ψ-Dependent Extensions:''' Content that only becomes meaningful if the ψ field hypothesis is experimentally confirmed. This includes ψ impedance matching, soliton state storage, and group coherence amplification. Track B content appears in sections labeled <code>== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==</code> on each page.

This separation is not a hedge — it is the discipline. A device that is buildable and measurable under Track A, and which produces anomalous results that Track A physics cannot explain, is the experimental gateway to Track B. The [[Mode Geometry Test]] is the designed experiment for this transition.

